|name = Gory
|image = E 006.png
|first appearance = '''EoC''': [[Madagascar (Empire of Cats)|Chapter 1 - Madagascar/Tottori]]<br>
'''SoL''': [[Gentle Smile|Sub-chapter 1 - Gentle Smile]]<br>
'''ItF''': [[China (Into the Future)|Chapter 1 - China]]<br>
'''CotC''': [[Deneb (Cats of the Cosmos)|Chapter 1 - Deneb]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Loony Lakeside|Sub-chapter 3 - Loony Lakeside]]
|money drop = 550¢ - 2,173¢
}}

==Enemy==
Gory has high speed, attack rate and DPS, along with Area Attack, making him essentially an upgraded [[Jackie Peng]].

==Strategy==
Groups of Gories can be deadly without a proper strategy. Fragile cats such as [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]] should not fight Gories without some help from [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]].

Gory is basically a faster version of Jackie Peng with Area Attack. Just like in [[Dubai (Empire of Cats)|Dubai/Hiroshima]], you face two of them in one battle. To deal with them, you may need the [[Energy Drink]] so you can get money faster.

In [[Empire of Cats]], the best way to kill a Gory quickly is to use 1-3 [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cats/Sexy Legs Cats]] and many [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cats/Macho Cats]] and [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cats/Brave Cats]] as meatshields or attackers that can knock the Gory back in 1 hit, like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat/Dragon Cat]]. Be sure to protect your longer-ranged cats with cheap cats like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat/Wall Cat]] and [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat/Samba Cat]].

Later on, Gory's threat level decreases drastically and he becomes a giant money bag, as even at higher strength magnifications, his stats leave too much to be desired for a melee pusher, making him no more than a glorified peon.

