==Trivia==
*"Gory" is an obvious play on "gorilla", the real animal he is based on.
*Gory and most of his variants are mocked by their descriptions for their scary faces, addictions and occasionally employment issues:
**[[Gory Dark]] is ironically an exception, with the 4koma "[https://app.famitsu.com/20140214_314143/ Working Black Gory-san]" (働くブラッゴリさん ''Hataraku Buraggori-san'') showing how Gory became Gory Dark. Meanwhile, [[Ragin' Gory]] was overworked by his exploitative employer and flew off the handle when he saw a new employee leaving without having to endure overtime like he did.
**[[Angelic Gory]] was pretty much the same as Gory, being dismissed from his position by his hideous face and also resorted to gambling.
**[[General GreGory]]'s Japanese description claims he is likely a shy individual who was chosen as a general merely due to his appearance. His English description instead cites his appearance as why he could not find a partner, but also mentions his talents and his reluctance in displaying them.
**[[Zory]]'s face got him banished from the netherworld, and, horrified by his [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|zombified]] self, he resumed gambling out of despair. His English description instead cites him being rejected from heaven.
**[[Aku Gory]]'s appearance was what got him scouted by the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]], but he was soon fired and became a streamer. His English description is more in line with how Angelic Gory was fired, and omits the part mentioning his unemployment.
**[[Angelic Beast Rajakong]], despite his intimidating appearance, is actually a gentle creature who dedicates his effort to environmentalism.
*[[Kory]] started freeloading at Gory's house after being kicked out from the zoo, though Gory plans to evict him soon.
*[[Nimoy Bore]]'s Japanese description states that Gory hates Nimoy Bore's gag of raising his hoof with cuticle hair. When Gory brought this up, Nimoy Bore went on a rampage out of shock.
*He is one of the few enemies to have both [[:Category:Unstarred Alien Enemies|unstarred]] and [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variants, the others being [[Doge]] and the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s.
*One of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] is "Gory will take away your best clients."

